# =============================================================================
# Repository-root environment reference
#
# This file documents what exists; it is NOT loaded by the applications.
#   - Browser variables live in apps/web/.env.example  -> apps/web/.env.local
#   - Server secrets are NOT stored in .env files at all.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE SECRETS: where they actually live
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud Functions read privileged values from GOOGLE SECRET MANAGER at runtime,
# bound per-function. They are never committed, never placed in a .env file, and
# never exposed to the browser.
#
# Secrets that will be created in Phase 4 (names only — no values, ever):
#   PAYMENT_GATEWAY_KEY_ID          # gateway publishable/merchant id
#   PAYMENT_GATEWAY_SECRET          # gateway secret key
#   PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET          # webhook signature verification secret
#   NOTIFICATION_EMAIL_API_KEY      # transactional email provider
#   NOTIFICATION_SMS_API_KEY        # SMS provider (if not Firebase-native)
#
# No payment provider has been selected and no credentials exist. These names are
# placeholders for planning only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVICE ACCOUNTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is NO service-account JSON anywhere in this repository, and there must
# never be one.
#   - Cloud Functions use the runtime default service account (no key file).
#   - Local development uses the Firebase Emulator Suite (no credentials at all).
#   - CI authenticates to Google Cloud via Workload Identity Federation, so no
#     long-lived key is stored in GitHub secrets either.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local emulator defaults (optional overrides)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8080
# FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:9099
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:9199
